outputs.exact_statement:
Let $Z$ be a projective $\mathbb Q$-factorial klt variety over $\mathbb C$, let $\Theta\geq0$ be a rational divisor, and let $V\subset Z$ be an integral positive-dimensional subvariety. Suppose that $(Z,\Theta)$ is lc at the generic point of $V$ and that a divisor of log discrepancy zero has center $V$. Let $f=\dim V$, let $P$ be a nef rational Cartier divisor on $Z$, and let $\rho:V^*\to V$ be a smooth projective resolution, factoring through the normalization. Then $$\label{eq:numerical-subadjunction}
 K_{V^*}\cdot(\rho^*P)^{f-1}
 \leq (K_Z+\Theta)|_V\cdot(P|_V)^{f-1}.$$ The right side is the intersection of the restricted rational Cartier class with the cycle $[V]$. No $\mathbb Q$-Gorenstein hypothesis on the normalization of $V$ is required.

Let $Z$ be a projective $\mathbb Q$-factorial klt variety of dimension $d$, let $P$ be an ample rational Cartier divisor, and let $k>0$ be an integer for which $kP$ is Cartier. Let $0\ne\mathcal H\subset H^0(Z,\mathcal O_Z(kP))$ be a linear subspace with proper base locus and base ideal $\mathfrak b$. Suppose that $V$ is an integral base-locus component of dimension $f<d$, isolated at its generic point $\eta_V$, and that $\eta_V\in Z_{\rm sm}$. Write $a=d-f$ and $\mathfrak m=\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O_{Z,\eta_V}}$. If $$\mathfrak b\mathcal O_{Z,\eta_V}\subset\mathfrak m^h
 \qquad(h\in\mathbb Z_{>0}),$$ then $$\label{eq:base-component-degree}
 P^f\cdot V\leq (k/h)^aP^d.$$ If $f>0$, there is a rational number $c$ with $0<c\leq ak/h$ such that, on a smooth resolution $V^*$, $$\label{eq:base-component-canonical}
 K_{V^*}\cdot P^{f-1}
 \leq (K_Z+cP)|_V\cdot P^{f-1}.$$ The coefficient $c$ may be chosen with an effective rational divisor $\Theta\sim_{\mathbb Q}cP$ such that $(Z,\Theta)$ is lc at the generic point of $V$ and has an lc place with center $V$. Thus can also be applied with a different nef testing class. The degree estimate includes $f=0$; the canonical estimate is asserted only for positive-dimensional $V$.

The varieties $Y\times Y$, $Z$, and $Z_{\mathrm{sl}}$ are projective, $\mathbb Q$-factorial, and klt. The tautological classes of the two bundles are nef, and $P$ and $P_{\mathrm{sl}}$ are ample rational divisors. Writing $K_\Sigma=K_1+K_2$ on the product and $K_\Sigma=K$ on a slice, one has $$\label{eq:two-slot-canonical}
 K_{\mathrm{bundle}}
 =-2\xi+(\iota+1)K_\Sigma
 \le\frac{\iota+1}{r_t}\,P_{\mathrm{bundle}}$$ in nef order.

Assume $q\iota/r_t\le1$. For sufficiently small $t$, there are positive constants $c_n,C_n$, depending only on $n$, such that $$\label{eq:two-slot-total-volume}
 c_n q\epsilon^{2n}\le P^d\le C_n q\epsilon^{2n}.$$ On either slice, $$\label{eq:two-slot-slice-volume}
 0<P_{\mathrm{sl}}^{\,n+1}
 \le2^{n+2}q\epsilon^n .$$

There is a strongly movable curve class $\gamma$ on $\widehat W$, represented as the pushforward of an ample complete intersection on a fixed smooth projective birational model, such that $$\label{eq:movable-test}
 (\pi_x^*D^+)\cdot\gamma
 <40\epsilon\,J_x\cdot\gamma,\qquad J_x\cdot\gamma>0.$$

Let $M=(m_{ij})\in\operatorname{Mat}_{w\times v}(\mathbb Q)$ and $d\in\mathbb Q^w$. If the system $$\label{eq:rational-feasibility}
 d_i-y_i=\sum_{j=1}^{v}m_{ij}b_j\quad(1\le i\le w),
 \qquad y_i\ge0$$ has a real solution, it has a rational solution. Moreover, one may require precisely the same $y_i$ to be zero as in the given solution. Consequently, if $D$ is a rational Weil divisor on a normal integral variety $X$ over a field $k$ and $D\sim_{\mathbb R}G$ for an effective real Weil divisor $G$, then $D\sim_{\mathbb Q}G_{\mathbb Q}$ for an effective rational divisor with $\mathop{\mathrm{Supp}}G_{\mathbb Q}=\mathop{\mathrm{Supp}}G$. If $rD$ is Cartier for a prescribed positive integer $r$, then $H^0(X,\mathcal O_X(mrD))\ne0$ for some $m>0$.
